  abstract          = {Technical and financial feasibility assessment of distributed solar PV systems for BP’s company-owned service station network (COCO) in Mexico. The study included load profiling for 62 pilot stations (~3.9 GWh/year), preliminary layout design using satellite-based site analysis, system sizing, and evaluation of compensation schemes (Equity vs. PPA). A 15-year financial projection model was developed to compare on-site generation versus grid procurement, incorporating CAPEX, tariff structures, savings, and long-term return scenarios. The project supported strategic decision-making toward decentralized renewable integration within a retail mobility network.},
